    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d299">

                <pb facs="0275" n="263" sameAs="frus:frus1942v04/pg263"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">741.9111/24: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Iran</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Dreyfus</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Tehran</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1942-01-12T16:00:00+03:25">January 12, 1942—4
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received January 12—5:36 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>7. I have advised the Iranian Government of the purport of Department’s 165,
                    December 29.<anchor n="41" xml:id="d299-f1"/> Both the Prime<anchor n="42"
                        xml:id="d299-f2"/> and Foreign Ministers<anchor n="43" xml:id="d299-f3"/>
                    seem deeply perturbed about the situation in Azerbaijan, alleging that Soviet
                    interference and propaganda continue unabated. They express the belief that this
                    condition might be alleviated and that the Russians might perhaps be deterred
                    from pushing a Separatist movement were the United States to make a statement
                    taking cognizance of the treaty<anchor n="44" xml:id="d299-f4"/> and
                    guaranteeing the independence and territorial integrity of Iran. The Foreign
                    Minister states that the Shah intends when treaty is signed, which should be in
                    a week or so, to communicate this fact to the President referring in his
                    communication to the Atlantic Charter.<anchor n="45" xml:id="d299-f5"/> The
                    reply to this telegram might present a good opportunity for a statement along
                    the lines suggested above, should the Department deem such a course to be
                    advisable. If such a statement is made in reply to the Shah’s telegrams the
                    Iranian Government would wish to have permission to publish it.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Dreyfus</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
